{"findings":[{"id":"R1","kind":"requirement","statement":"The host creates one dinner question with a fixed set of 2–8 place options before voting starts.","basis":["scenario.workflow[0]","scenario.objective","trusted_source_ids.requirements.flow-1"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"R2","kind":"requirement","statement":"Members vote on the same device under a self-chosen code (pseudonym), one option per person; re-submitting with the same code replaces the earlier choice so a person still holds exactly one vote.","basis":["scenario.audience","scenario.workflow[1]","scenario.workflow[2]","acceptance[0]","product_shape_guidance"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"R3","kind":"requirement","statement":"A per-option tally is the visible deliverable: two people on different options must show total 2 with 1/1, and after one changes vote still total 2 (0/2).","basis":["scenario.objective","acceptance[0]"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"R4","kind":"requirement","statement":"The host can close the poll; after closing, further votes return poll_closed and the stored result is unchanged. The host can reopen, after which a third member can vote for a total of 3.","basis":["scenario.workflow[3]","scenario.workflow[4]","acceptance[1]"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"R5","kind":"requirement","statement":"A vote option must belong to the poll being voted on; duplicate options and an empty code must be rejected, and votes from different polls must never be merged.","basis":["acceptance[2]"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"R6","kind":"requirement","statement":"Poll state and aggregate must survive a page refresh and a process restart in the same directory, and a tie must be displayed as a tie rather than resolved by an arbitrary winner.","basis":["acceptance[3]","scenario.workflow[4]"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"O1","kind":"observation","statement":"The upstream product is a Nextcloud server application written in PHP and JS/Vue, positioned as a free meeting-schedule tool similar to Doodle, not a standalone same-device poll page.","basis":["README.md:5","README.md:20","source-2"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"O2","kind":"observation","statement":"The poll entity has exactly two declared poll types, datePoll and textPoll, plus a 'simple' voting variant; the model is oriented to date/text option scheduling rather than a generic single-choice question.","basis":["lib/Db/Poll.php:88-90"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"O3","kind":"observation","statement":"A vote is stored per option as an answer of yes, no, or maybe, not as a single selected option; the poll carries allowMaybe and useNo settings that govern those answer modes.","basis":["lib/Db/Vote.php:39-41","lib/Db/Vote.php:44-51","lib/Db/Poll.php:154","lib/Db/Poll.php:163"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"O4","kind":"observation","statement":"Votes are soft-deleted rows carrying pollId, userId, option id, a snapshot of the option text, an option hash, and the answer, so a vote row is bound to a poll and an option record rather than to a free-text answer.","basis":["lib/Db/Vote.php:45-51","lib/Db/Vote.php:110-122"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"O5","kind":"observation","statement":"Option identity in the vote is cryptographically derived from the poll id plus the option text, and a separate accessor exposes the raw stored hash so mismatches between text and hash can be detected.","basis":["lib/Db/Vote.php:77-103"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"O6","kind":"observation","statement":"Poll lifecycle is driven by an integer expiry timestamp: a poll is expired when expire > 0 and expire < now, and voting is denied whenever the poll is expired. No explicit open/closed boolean or reopen field appears in the supplied Poll entity.","basis":["lib/Db/Poll.php:39-40","lib/Db/Poll.php:396-404","lib/Db/Poll.php:1007-1008"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"O7","kind":"observation","statement":"Archival is separate from closing: a deleted timestamp marks the poll archived, and the entity distinguishes isArchived from isExpired in its status payload.","basis":["lib/Db/Poll.php:151","lib/Db/Poll.php:285-286"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"O8","kind":"observation","statement":"Result visibility is a three-way poll setting (always, closed, never); editors always see results, participants see them only per the setting, and the legacy value 'expired' is mapped to 'closed'.","basis":["lib/Db/Poll.php:93-95","lib/Db/Poll.php:594-597","lib/Db/Poll.php:1026-1043"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"O9","kind":"observation","statement":"Participation identity is a Nextcloud user identity: the poll stores an owner user id, each vote stores a userId, and voting is restricted to external, user, or admin user types (other external types must register first).","basis":["lib/Db/Poll.php:148","lib/Db/Vote.php:46","lib/Db/Poll.php:996-1000"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"O10","kind":"observation","statement":"Anonymity is a poll setting with a lockable state: a negative anonymous value means real anonymous and is treated as locked so the setting cannot be changed back.","basis":["lib/Db/Poll.php:287","lib/Db/Poll.php:457-475"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"O11","kind":"observation","statement":"Access and roles are granular: access is private or open, roles include owner/admin/user/email/contact/external/none, and there are more than twenty named permissions covering edit, vote, see results, see usernames, add options, comment, share, download, deanonymize, and change foreign votes.","basis":["lib/Db/Poll.php:91-92","lib/Db/Poll.php:106-136","lib/Db/Poll.php:343-367"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"O12","kind":"observation","statement":"Changing another participant's votes and deanonymizing are separately gated privileges tied to edit rights, an unrestricted poll owner, and an unlocked anonymity setting.","basis":["lib/Db/Poll.php:967-985"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"O13","kind":"observation","statement":"Option creation by participants is a configurable proposal mode (disallow, allow, review) with an optional proposal expiry, and public shares are explicitly barred from adding options.","basis":["lib/Db/Poll.php:96-98","lib/Db/Poll.php:861-894"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"O14","kind":"observation","statement":"Vote volume controls exist as maxVotesPerUser and maxVotesPerOption, i.e. limits on votes, not a limit on the number of poll options.","basis":["lib/Db/Poll.php:313-314","lib/Db/Poll.php:157-158","README.md:27"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"O15","kind":"observation","statement":"Cloning a poll produces a private, deanonymized copy titled 'Clone of …' with settings carried over and no votes; deletion/archive supports an auto-delete offset in days.","basis":["lib/Db/Poll.php:215-256","lib/Db/Poll.php:635-640"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"O16","kind":"observation","statement":"Documented product-level capabilities include hiding results, obfuscating participant names, automatic expiry, participant-added options, per-option/per-user vote limits, invitations, export to spreadsheet/HTML, reminders, comments, confirming options after closing, notifications, calendar conflict hints, and a REST API.","basis":["README.md:23-36"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"O17","kind":"observation","statement":"The README states the app is not maintained by Nextcloud despite living in the Nextcloud GitHub organisation, and its screenshots describe managing/creating polls, many configuration options, sharing a poll, and voting on mobile.","basis":["README.md:51","README.md:63-66"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"O18","kind":"observation","statement":"Licensing is GNU AGPL version 3 (COPYING text) with SPDX-License-Identifier: AGPL-3.0-or-later headers in the supplied PHP files; the snapshot records license status as fixed_notice_located_spdx_not_independently_verified.","basis":["COPYING:1-2","lib/Db/Poll.php:4-7","lib/Db/Vote.php:4-7","source/snapshot.json"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"O19","kind":"observation","statement":"Upstream was not executed: the snapshot records upstream_status = not_run, so every upstream statement here is a static reading of the pinned files, not an observed behavior.","basis":["source/snapshot.json","input.json:adapter.stage"],"confidence":"high"},{"id":"D1","kind":"design_choice","statement":"Model closing/reopening as an explicit poll status transition owned by the host, instead of reusing an expiry timestamp as the only way to stop voting; store close and reopen events so a closed poll rejects writes with poll_closed and a reopened poll accepts new voters.","rationale":"Upstream couples stoppage to expire and has no reopen field in the supplied entity; the scenario requires manual close and explicit reopen.","confidence":"high"},{"id":"D2","kind":"design_choice","statement":"Represent a ballot as (poll id, pseudonym code, single option id) with uniqueness on (poll id, code); a re-vote by the same code replaces that ballot rather than appending a second one, and the aggregate is recomputed from ballots.","rationale":"Upstream's per-option yes/no/maybe rows with user ids do not satisfy one-person-one-choice on a shared device.","confidence":"high"},{"id":"D3","kind":"design_choice","statement":"Give options stable poll-scoped ids and validate that a submitted option id belongs to the submitted poll; normalize labels and reject duplicates and empty option labels at creation.","rationale":"Binds the scenario's option-membership and duplicate/empty rejection rules to identity rather than free text.","confidence":"high"},{"id":"D4","kind":"design_choice","statement":"Use a single durable local store in the application directory with atomic writes, and derive totals from stored ballots on load so refresh and restart reproduce identical state.","rationale":"Scenario requires same-directory process restart persistence; no server database or account layer is in scope.","confidence":"high"},{"id":"D5","kind":"design_choice","statement":"Display ties as equal counts with all tied options listed and no winner designation, and never synthesize a tiebreaker.","rationale":"Explicit acceptance rule; differs from any winner-oriented framing.","confidence":"high"},{"id":"D6","kind":"design_choice","statement":"Separate host surface (create poll, set options, close, reopen, view tally) from participant surface (enter code, select one option, submit, see current tally), both usable sequentially on one device without per-member accounts.","rationale":"product_shape_guidance calls for pseudonyms and host/member actions with no remote authentication platform.","confidence":"high"},{"id":"D7","kind":"design_choice","statement":"Borrow upstream's configurability ideas only where they map to this scenario (result visibility during/after voting, one-vote-per-person enforcement); do not import Nextcloud accounts, shares, groups, REST API, reminders, comments, or calendar integration.","rationale":"Keeps the product inside the leaf's defining core and out of scheduling/survey territory.","confidence":"high"},{"id":"U1","kind":"unknown","statement":"How the upstream aggregate is computed and displayed (counts, percentages, chart, tie presentation) cannot be determined: no tally, mapper, controller, or frontend file is in the supplied inventory.","status":"unknown","confidence":"high"},{"id":"U2","kind":"unknown","statement":"Upstream reopen-after-close behavior is unknown; the supplied entity exposes only expire and deleted, and no reopen action was read.","status":"unknown","confidence":"high"},{"id":"U3","kind":"unknown","statement":"Whether upstream supports same-device sequential voting under self-declared pseudonyms without accounts is unknown and is contradicted by the user-type gate on voting; no such path appears in the supplied files.","status":"unknown","confidence":"medium"},{"id":"U4","kind":"unknown","statement":"Upstream rejection of duplicate option labels, empty option labels, or empty participant identifiers is not evidenced in the supplied files.","status":"unknown","confidence":"high"},{"id":"U5","kind":"unknown","statement":"No upstream rule limiting a poll to 2–8 options was found; the discovered limits apply to votes per user and votes per option.","status":"unknown","confidence":"high"},{"id":"U6","kind":"unknown","statement":"Runtime behavior, persistence across restarts, and any error code such as poll_closed were not executed or observed upstream (upstream_status not_run).","status":"not_run","confidence":"high"},{"id":"G1","kind":"observation","statement":"The supplied upstream inventory is four files only (COPYING, README.md, lib/Db/Poll.php, lib/Db/Vote.php); entity definitions are visible but routing, controllers, services, mappers, migrations, and frontend are absent.","basis":["source/snapshot.json","input.json:trusted_source_ids.upstream"],"confidence":"high"}],"observed_upstream":[["doc","README.md",5,5,"# Polls - an app, similar to doodle or DuD-Poll, for Nextcloud written in PHP and JS/Vue."],["doc","README.md",20,20,"# Free meeting schedule tool"],["doc","README.md",23,23,"    - :envelope: Make your poll confidential by hiding the results until you want them to be discovered"],["doc","README.md",24,24,"    - :dark_sunglasses: Obfuscate participants' names from other participants or set strong anonymous mode"],["doc","README.md",25,25,"    - :timer_clock: Set an automatic expiry date"],["doc","README.md",26,26,"    - :heavy_plus_sign: Allow participants to add more options"],["doc","README.md",27,27,"    - :white_check_mark: Limit votes per option or user"],["doc","README.md",30,30,"- :rocket: Export your poll to different spreadsheet formats or HTML"],["doc","README.md",33,33,"- :ballot_box_with_check: Confirm options after poll closing"],["doc","README.md",36,36,"- :toolbox: Usable via REST-API"],["doc","README.md",51,51,"For clarification: Polls is not maintained by Nextcloud, although it resides unter the Nextcloud organisation here on Github."],["doc","README.md",64,64,"Manage your polls and create new ones | Many configuration options | Share your poll with other peopl